#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:-1
msgid "The HEIF and AVIF file formats in Krita."
msgstr "Les formats de fichiers « HEIF » et « AVIF » dans Krita."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:10
msgid "High Efficiency Image Format"
msgstr "Format d'image à haute efficacité"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:10
msgid "AV1 Image Format"
msgstr "Format d'image « AV1 »"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:10
msgid "\\*.heif"
msgstr "\\*.heif"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:10
msgid "\\*.avif"
msgstr "\\*.avif"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:10
msgid "\\*.heic"
msgstr "\\*.heic"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:10
msgid "hdr"
msgstr "hdr"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:10
msgid "AVIF"
msgstr "AVIF"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:10
msgid "HEIF"
msgstr "HEIF"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:10
msgid "HEIC"
msgstr "HEIC"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:16
msgid "\\*.heif and \\*.avif"
msgstr "\\*.heif et \\*.avif"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:18
msgid ""
"The High Efficiency Image Format (``*.heif``, ``*.heic``), and its cousin, "
"AV1 Image Format (``*.avif``) are formats which use video codecs (``H264``, "
"``H265`` and ``AV1``) to store their data. They are more and more popular "
"with mobile phones as their default image file format, and ``*.avif`` is to "
"be natively supported by all web browsers within the next few years."
msgstr ""

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:20
msgid ""
"Krita supports saving :ref:`model_gray` and :ref:`model_rgb` images to these "
"formats. Furthermore, it can save 8 bit, will save 16 bit integer as 12 bit, "
"and can save 16 and 32 bit float as 12 bit, with an HDR color space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:22
msgid ""
"Compared to :ref:`file_png` and :ref:`file_jpeg`, these formats tend to "
"smooth out textures to make them easier to compress, and therefore great for "
"sharp images with a lot of smooth gradients. Images with a lot of texture or "
"fine details may lose said detail (for example, cat whiskers seem to get "
"lost), and thus :ref:`file_jpeg` might be better suited."
msgstr ""

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:25
msgid "Import Options"
msgstr "Importer des options"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:27
msgid ""
"Krita supports all the color spaces that these formats can handle, and will "
"convert in the case of the few formats it cannot handle. This has been "
"automated for the most part, with Krita selecting or generating the "
"appropriate ICC profile where necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:29
msgid ""
"Images that are HDR images, so the ones that have the Perceptual Quantizer, "
"Hybrid Log Gamma or SMPTE ST 428 transfer functions, will be converted to a "
"linear 32 bit floating point version of that color space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:31
msgid ""
"However, Hybrid Log Gamma needs an extra conversion step inbetween, as Krita "
"currently does not support sending HLG data to the display. For this :dfn:"
"`Scene Linear to Display Linear` conversion, it would need to know your :dfn:"
"`display gamma` and :dfn:`maximum brightness`. The default brightness and "
"gamma values are the ones used for a HLG to PQ conversion, and probably your "
"best bet when your monitor is able to display Krita's HDR. When exporting "
"this image with HLG, it's recommended to reuse the same values for the "
"reverse OOTF there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:33
msgid "Apply Hybrid Log Gamma OOTF"
msgstr "Appliquer un gamma logarithmique hybride « OOTF »"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:34
msgid ""
"Whether to apply the extra conversion step. This will convert scene linear "
"values to display linear, and thus it's necessity is completely dependent on "
"your HDR workflow. If in doubt, apply."
msgstr ""
"S'il faut appliquer l'étape de conversion supplémentaire. Cette étape "
"convertira les valeurs linéaires de la scène en valeurs linéaires pour "
"l'affichage. Ensuite, cette nécessité dépend donc entièrement de votre flux "
"de travail « HDR ». En cas de doute, appliquez-la."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:35
#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:82
msgid "Gamma"
msgstr "Gamma"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:36
#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:83
msgid "Approximate display gamma. Default value is 1.2 for conversion to PQ."
msgstr ""
"Réaliser une approximation pour le gamma d'affichage. La valeur par défaut "
"est de 1.2 pour la conversion en « PQ »."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:38
#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:85
msgid "Brightness"
msgstr "Luminosité"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:38
#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:85
msgid ""
"Maximum display brightness. Default value is 10.000 cd/m² for conversion to "
"PQ."
msgstr ""
"Luminosité maximale de l'écran. La valeur par défaut est de 10.000 cd / m² "
"pour la conversion en « PQ »."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:41
msgid "Export Options"
msgstr "Exporter des options"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:43
msgid "Lossless"
msgstr "Sans perte"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:44
msgid ""
"Use the lossless encoding options. Disables the :guilabel:`Lossy Advanced "
"Settings`."
msgstr ""
"Utiliser les options d'encodage sans perte. Désactive les :guilabel:"
"`Paramètres avancés sans perte`."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:46
msgid "Lossy Advanced Settings"
msgstr "Configuration avancée pour méthode sans perte"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:46
msgid "Quality"
msgstr "Qualité"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:47
msgid ""
"Determines how much the encoder should prioritize quality over compression. "
"Higher values look better, but lower values have a lower file size."
msgstr ""
"Détermine dans quelle mesure l'encodeur doit privilégier la qualité par "
"rapport à la compression. Les valeurs plus élevées conduisent à un meilleur "
"aspect, mais les valeurs plus basses permettent d'avoir des fichiers moins "
"volumineux."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:49
msgid ""
"Chroma Subsampling settings. Humans are more sensitive to the brightness of "
"an image than its colorfulness, so halving the colors of an image can be a "
"very useful way to compress an image. This is best used with images that "
"have few sharp contrasts, as that is where the reduced resolution is most "
"obvious."
msgstr ""

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:51
msgid "420"
msgstr "420"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:52
msgid ""
"The brightness of the image will be at full resolution, while the "
"colorfulness will be halved in both dimensions."
msgstr ""
"La luminosité de l'image sera à pleine résolution, tandis que la richesse "
"des couleurs sera réduite de moitié dans les deux dimensions."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:53
msgid "422"
msgstr "422"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:54
msgid ""
"The brightness of the image will be at full resolution, while the "
"colorfulness will be halved horizontally."
msgstr ""
"La luminosité de l'image sera à pleine résolution, tandis que la "
"colorimétrie sera divisée par deux horizontalement."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:56
msgid "Chroma"
msgstr "Chrominance"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:56
msgid "444"
msgstr "444"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:56
msgid ""
"Both brightness and colorfulness of the image will be at full resolution."
msgstr ""
"La luminosité et les couleurs de l'image, à la fois, seront en pleine "
"résolution."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:59
msgid "Conversion Settings"
msgstr "Configuration de conversion"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:61
msgid ""
"These only appear on floating point images, and are used to store the images "
"with values above 1.0 as HDR images by encoding them with a specific "
"transfer function."
msgstr ""
"Ils n'apparaissent que sur les images à virgule flottante. Ils sont utilisés "
"pour enregistrer des images dont les valeurs sont supérieures à 1,0 en tant "
"qu'images « HDR » en les encodant avec une fonction de transfert spécifique."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:64
msgid ""
"Encoding the right color space depends on how compatible the current color "
"space is with the ``ITU H.273 CICP`` values [ituh273]_, as this is how "
"``PQ``, ``HLG`` and ``SMPTE ST 428`` are stored. ``Rec 2100 PQ`` or ``Rec "
"2100 HLG`` are the expected values for HDR images [rec2100]_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:66
msgid ""
"In all cases when we store ``CICP`` values instead of an ICC profile, the "
"Matrix Coefficient value will be set to 0 (Identity Matrix), as Krita does "
"no conversion to ``YUV``."
msgstr ""
"Dans tous les cas où nous stockons des valeurs « CICP » au lieu d'un profil "
"« ICC », la valeur du coefficient de matrice sera mise à 0 (matrice "
"d'identité). En effet, Krita ne fait pas de conversion en « YUV »."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:68
msgid "Rec 2100 PQ"
msgstr "Rec 2100 PQ"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:69
msgid ""
"Image will first be converted to Rec 2020 linear. Then encoded with the "
"Perceptual Quantizer function (also known as ``SMPTE 2048`` curve). This is "
"the most common HDR encoding, and useful for images where the relative "
"brightness is important."
msgstr ""

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:70
msgid "Rec 2100 HLG"
msgstr "Rec 2100 HLG"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:71
msgid ""
"Image will first be converted to Rec 2020 linear. Then encoded with the "
"Hybrid Log Gamma function, and finally, if chosen, the reverse Hybrid Log "
"Gamma OOTF is applied. This is useful for images where the final display may "
"not understand PQ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:72
msgid "Keep Colorants, encode PQ"
msgstr "Conserver les colorants. Encoder en « PQ »."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:73
msgid ""
"Shows only for images with an ``ITU H.273`` compatible color space "
"[ituh273]_. The image will be linearized first, and then encoded with a "
"perceptual quantizer curve."
msgstr ""
"Ne s'affiche que pour les images avec un espace colorimétrique compatible "
"« ITU H.273 » [ituh273]_. L'image sera d'abord linéarisée, puis encodée avec "
"une courbe de quantification perceptuelle."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:74
msgid "Keep Colorants, encode HLG"
msgstr "Conserver les colorants. Encoder « HLG »."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:75
msgid ""
"Shows only for images with an ``ITU H.273`` compatible color space "
"[ituh273]_. The image will be linearized first, and then encoded with a "
"Hybrid Log Gamma curve. Finally, the reverse HLG OOTF may be applied."
msgstr ""
"Ne s'affiche que pour les images avec un espace colorimétrique compatible "
"avec la norme « ITU H.273 »[ituh273]_. L'image sera d'abord linéarisée, puis "
"encodée avec une courbe de gamma logarithmique hybride. Enfin, l'OOTF HLG "
"inverse pourrait être appliqué."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:76
msgid "Keep Colorants, encode SMPTE ST 428"
msgstr "Conserver les colorants. Encoder en « SMPTE ST 428 »."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:77
msgid ""
"Shows only for images with an ``ITU H.273`` compatible color space "
"[ituh273]_. The image will be linearized first, and then encoded with "
"``SMPTE ST 428``. Krita always opens images like these as linear floating "
"point, this option is there to save them as ``ST 428`` again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:78
msgid "Space:"
msgstr "Espace :"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:78
msgid "No Changes, Clip"
msgstr "Aucune modification. Couper"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:79
msgid ""
"The image will be converted plainly to 12bit integer, and values that are "
"out of bounds are clipped, the ICC profile will be embedded."
msgstr ""
"L'image sera convertie en totalité sur 12 bits. Les valeurs hors limites "
"seront supprimées et le profil « ICC » sera intégré."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:80
msgid "Apply reverse Hybrid Log Gamma OOTF"
msgstr "Appliquer un gamma inverse logarithmique hybride « OOTF »"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:81
msgid ""
"Whether to apply the extra conversion step. It's necessity is completely "
"dependent on your HDR workflow. If in doubt, apply, always apply when you've "
"imported an image with OOTF option enabled."
msgstr ""
"S'il faut appliquer l'étape de conversion supplémentaire. Cette nécessité "
"dépend entièrement de votre flux de travail « HDR ». En cas de doute, "
"appliquez. Appliquez la toujours lorsque vous avez importé une image avec "
"l'option « OOTF » activée."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:89
msgid ""
"`High Efficiency Image File Format on Wikipedia <https://en.wikipedia.org/"
"wiki/High_Efficiency_Image_File_Format>`_"
msgstr ""
"« Format de fichier « HEIF » (High Efficiency Image File) sur Wikipedia "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Efficiency_Image_File_Format> »_"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:91
msgid ""
"`H.273 : Coding-independent code points for video signal type identification "
"<https://www.itu.int/rec/T-REC-H.273/en>`_"
msgstr ""
"« H.273 : points de code indépendants du codage pour l'identification du "
"type de signal vidéo <https://www.itu.int/rec/T-REC-H.273/en> »_"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:93
msgid ""
"`BT.2100 : Image parameter values for high dynamic range television for use "
"in production and international programme exchange <https://www.itu.int/rec/"
"R-REC-BT.2100-2-201807-I/en>`_"
msgstr ""
"« BT.2100 : valeurs des paramètres d'image pour la télévision à haute gamme "
"dynamique pour utilisation dans la production et l'échange international de "
"programmes <https://www.itu.int/rec/R-REC-BT.2100-2-201807-I/en> »_."

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:94
msgid ""
"`Perceptual Quantizer on Wikipedia <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Perceptual_quantizer>`_"
msgstr ""
"« Quantificateur perceptuel sur Wikipedia <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Perceptual_quantizer> »_"

#: ../../general_concepts/file_formats/file_heif.rst:95
msgid ""
"`Hybrid Log Gamma on Wikipedia <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hybrid_log"
"%E2%80%93gamma>`_"
msgstr ""
"« Gamma logarithmique hybride sur Wikipedia <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Hybrid_log%E2%80%93gamma> »_"
